meta {
  name: Select Patient (/agenda/select-patient)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/agenda/select-patient?patientId={{firstAgendaPatientId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
}

settings {
  followRedirects: false
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 302
  res.headers.location: eq /index.html
}

docs {
  UC-6 (REQUIREMENTS.md): the roster drill-down - hands one patient off from the agenda to that patient's
  own single-patient session (REQUIREMENTS.md UC-6's "opening any one patient from the list drops into that
  patient's own live conversational session"). `patientId` comes from Daily Agenda.bru's
  `firstAgendaPatientId`, run immediately before this in the same collection run (Bruno's
  `vars:post-response`), so this needs the agenda's roster to have at least one row for today - an
  empty demo-data agenda makes this 403 (not in roster) rather than a session-gate failure; seed at
  least one appointment for the launched clinician first (DEPLOYMENT.md §4a) if that happens.

  On success, AgendaEndpoints.HandleSelectPatientAsync saves a PatientSessionContext into the same
  session the Cookie header carries - Patient Context.bru (../Patient/) reuses that same
  `sessionCookie` and needs no separate launch. Expects a 302 to the chat SPA
  (`Bff:ChatPath`/index.html); redirect-following is disabled to see the raw response.
}
